// ============================================================================
// DAILY — 2026-11-12 (Thursday): Pure math sequence — Golomb's self-describing
// sequence (OEIS A001462, "the sequence that describes itself")
// ============================================================================
//
// THE SEQUENCE: a(1) = 1. a(n) = the number of times n occurs in the
// sequence itself. That single rule generates every term — verified against
// the OEIS entry, not invented: a(1)=1, a(2)=2, a(3)=2, a(4)=3, a(5)=3,
// a(6)=4, a(7)=4. Expanded, that reads: the value 1 appears once, 2 appears
// twice, 3 appears twice, 4 appears three times, 5 appears three times,
// 6 appears four times, 7 appears four times:
//   1, 2,2, 3,3, 4,4,4, 5,5,5, 6,6,6,6, 7,7,7,7
//
// PITCH + RHYTHM, read straight off that structure, no transform: each VALUE
// n (1..7) becomes scale degree n-1, and the COUNT a(n) — how many times
// that value legally occurs — becomes the literal `!count` repeat on that
// note. "6 appears four times" is heard as the 6th-degree note struck four
// times in a row, not described in a comment — the self-reference is the
// rhythm. One Golomb value per cycle (7 cycles total), so the piece is
// structured exactly like reading the sequence's own run-length groups
// aloud, one group per breath.
//
// JAZZ-IMPROV DEVICE — anchoring + arc: degree 0 (cycle 1, a single struck
// tonic) is the anchor/vadi the piece departs from and never returns to —
// deliberately, because the real sequence never resets either, it only
// grows. Each cycle both steps up by scale degree AND adds a repeat (1,2,2,
// 3,3,4,4), so pitch-rise and rhythmic-density-rise climb together: a single
// accelerating arc, not a repeated loop, which is the phrase development
// this topic asks for (contrast the flat "one loop restated" failure mode
// in MUSIC-QC-LOOP.md).
//
// ARRANGEMENT — two voices, each stating a DIFFERENT half of the same
// self-reference, because that's literally what the sequence is about (a
// value, and a count of that value):
//   - $lead (sawtooth): states the VALUE as pitch and the COUNT as repeat-
//     strikes, per cycle, as above. Bright/digital timbre (MUSIC-KNOWLEDGE.md
//     §1 — sawtooth = full harmonic series, "edge" — fitting a sequence
//     defined by counting, not a melodic topic).
//   - $drone (sine, soft): one long tone per cycle on the tonic, but its
//     lowpass cutoff climbs in 7 discrete steps, one per cycle — it is
//     literally counting "which number n we're currently on" while the lead
//     counts "how many times n occurs". Sine chosen deliberately against
//     the lead's sawtooth: pure vs. edgy, so the two self-describing halves
//     stay perceptually separate instead of fusing into one blended voice
//     (MUSIC-KNOWLEDGE.md §2, contrast not blend).
// This is a different arrangement idea from last Thursday's piece
// (2026-11-05, look-and-say): that one was a single growing-delay voice;
// this one is two voices in deliberate contrast, picked because THIS
// sequence's defining property is a pair (value, count-of-value), not a
// single generative growth process.
//
// NO DRUM LAYER: a counting sequence has no inherent metric pulse to track
// — it is not a beat, it's an index. The thing that "needs an audible
// outlet" here (the count a(n)) already gets one, directly, as the lead's
// own repeat-strikes; reaching for a kick/hat grid on top would just
// duplicate that information in a different register (see the 09-08/09-09
// percussion-as-default warning in MUSIC-QC-LOOP.md).
//
// TEMPO: setcpm(20) -> one cycle = 3s. CYCLES: 7 (one per Golomb group).
// 7 * 60 / 20 = 21s.
// ============================================================================

setcpm(20)

$lead: n("<0 [1!2] [2!2] [3!3] [4!3] [5!4] [6!4]>")
  .scale("C:dorian")
  .sound("sawtooth")
  .attack(.005).decay(.09).sustain(.08).release(.12)
  .lpf("<900 1100 1300 1600 2000 2500 3200>")
  .lpq(6)
  .delaytime(.12)
  .delayfeedback(.25)
  .delay(.3)
  .room(.3)
  .gain(.45)

$drone: n("0")
  .scale("C:dorian")
  .sound("sine")
  .attack(.3).decay(.2).sustain(.7).release(1.2)
  .lpf("<450 600 780 1000 1300 1650 2100>")
  .lpq(2)
  .gain(.28)
  .room(.5)
